{"name":"Méi Hēi Coal","hex":"#123120","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A black or brownish black rock formed from prehistoric plant remains, composed largely of carbon and burned as a fuel.","A type of coal, such as bituminous, anthracite, or lignite, and grades and varieties thereof, as a fuel commodity ready to buy and burn."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take on a supply of coal (usually of steam ships or locomotives).","To supply with coal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Prunus mume","blocks":[{"text":"Prunus mume, known by the common name Chinese plum, is a species of tree in the rose family. It is also referenced by its flowers as plum blossom. Despite being referred to as a plum, it is classified in the Armeniaca section of Prunus, making it an apricot."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Prunus_mume.JPG/330px-Prunus_mume.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prunus_mume"},{"title":"Coal","blocks":[{"text":"Coal is a combustible black or brownish-black sedimentary rock, formed as layers called coal seams. Coal is mostly carbon with variable amounts of other elements, chiefly hydrogen, sulfur, oxygen, and nitrogen. It is a fossil fuel, formed when plants decay into peat which is converted into coal by the heat and pressure of deep burial over millions of years. Vast deposits formed from wetlands called coal forests that covered much of the tropics during the late Carboniferous and early Permian."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Bituminous_Coal.JPG/330px-Bituminous_Coal.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coal"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Prunus_mume_fruits_2.jpg/120px-